1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:15,560
A biblical theology of generosity does not start with tithing, or even Jesus' command

2
00:00:15,560 --> 00:00:17,040
to be generous to the poor.

3
00:00:17,040 --> 00:00:25,880
It starts before time and space, with who God is.

4
00:00:27,020 --> 00:00:33,760
Since the beginning of Scripture, the world itself was created as an act of generous love,

5
00:00:33,760 --> 00:00:40,280
with God as a joyful, generous host, the world as His home,

6
00:00:40,280 --> 00:00:46,280
and you and I as His special guests.

7
00:00:46,280 --> 00:00:56,880
And from the inner nature of God, giving becomes our nature.

8
00:00:57,020 --> 00:01:05,480
And little by little, He makes our souls incandescent.

9
00:01:05,480 --> 00:01:31,260
Well, good morning, everyone.

10
00:01:32,680 --> 00:01:34,060
I hope you all are doing well.

11
00:01:34,060 --> 00:01:36,340
If we haven't had the privilege of meeting yet, my name is Ryan,

12
00:01:36,340 --> 00:01:40,720
and I have the privilege of being one of the pastors here at Canvas Community Church.

13
00:01:40,720 --> 00:01:45,760
And last week, we started our third Practicing the Way practice.

14
00:01:45,760 --> 00:01:51,220
If you're not familiar, Practicing the Way is a church-wide curriculum that we are using within our small groups

15
00:01:51,220 --> 00:01:55,680
aimed at helping us become more obedient disciples of Jesus.

16
00:01:55,680 --> 00:02:02,420
And one of Jesus' most famous sermons, He ends the sermon by saying,

17
00:02:02,420 --> 00:02:06,500
blessed are those who hear these words and put them into practice.

18
00:02:06,500 --> 00:02:12,740
We do not want to be a church who hears the teachings of Jesus, agrees with the teachings of Jesus,

19
00:02:12,740 --> 00:02:15,240
and goes out to lunch and forgets all about it.

20
00:02:15,680 --> 00:02:23,920
We want to be a church of people who take serious the commands of Jesus and through a personal relationship with the Holy Spirit,

21
00:02:23,920 --> 00:02:29,720
look to apply them the way that God is calling them, you and me and us, to apply them.

22
00:02:29,720 --> 00:02:38,380
These practices are not meant to be legalistic requirements to gain some kind of added level of holiness before God.

23
00:02:38,860 --> 00:02:42,640
These are invitations into a deeper personal relationship with God.

24
00:02:42,640 --> 00:02:48,440
And so don't do them if you're just doing them because you think you're supposed to do them to be a good person.

25
00:02:48,440 --> 00:02:56,640
Actually, Jesus has some of the harshest words to say to the Pharisees who are literally so good at doing all of the rules.

26
00:02:56,640 --> 00:02:59,960
They're better than you can ever be at doing the rules.

27
00:02:59,960 --> 00:03:06,160
And Jesus looks at them and gives them some strict, severe warnings because the rules are not the point.

28
00:03:06,480 --> 00:03:11,980
The point is the relationship and the whole person heart transformation.

29
00:03:11,980 --> 00:03:16,500
So that's what we're after with the Practicing the Way series.

30
00:03:16,500 --> 00:03:19,580
And this practice in particular is about generosity.

31
00:03:19,580 --> 00:03:25,920
And I, if you weren't here last week, I gave some disclaimers about money sermons in churches.

32
00:03:25,920 --> 00:03:30,300
So if you missed those disclaimers, I will, I'm sorry.

33
00:03:33,100 --> 00:03:35,920
I, I love to talk about money in church.

34
00:03:35,920 --> 00:03:37,700
Church should talk about money all the time.

35
00:03:37,700 --> 00:03:41,300
Actually, the more you give to our church, the more God, I'm just kidding.

36
00:03:41,300 --> 00:03:43,960
That was not the disclaimer.

37
00:03:43,960 --> 00:03:48,380
The disclaimer is the church has often done a bad job talking about money.

38
00:03:48,380 --> 00:03:53,760
And I just want to make it clear from the outset as we are addressing the topic of money and generosity,

39
00:03:54,760 --> 00:03:58,480
that the goal of this series is not that you would give us more of your money.

40
00:03:58,480 --> 00:04:00,320
We're doing pretty well.

41
00:04:00,320 --> 00:04:01,380
We're paying our bills.

42
00:04:01,380 --> 00:04:02,780
God is gracious.

43
00:04:02,780 --> 00:04:08,700
And when Jesus talks about money, I want you to know very clearly that Jesus does not need your money.

44
00:04:08,700 --> 00:04:10,360
Actually, all of your money is already his.

45
00:04:10,360 --> 00:04:15,440
That he's inviting you to use them in alignment with his kingdom.

46
00:04:16,120 --> 00:04:20,400
And that he's doing that not to take from you, but actually to give to you.

47
00:04:20,400 --> 00:04:27,880
That the teachings of Jesus are going to sound harsh and difficult and challenging to many of us in the room.

48
00:04:27,880 --> 00:04:30,720
And it's because we've been more discipled by our culture.

49
00:04:30,720 --> 00:04:34,280
And the idea is that our stuff is our stuff.

50
00:04:34,280 --> 00:04:38,020
And we deserve to get to use it how we want to use it.

51
00:04:38,020 --> 00:04:40,560
And nothing could be further from the truth.

52
00:04:40,560 --> 00:04:48,900
And so when Jesus invites us into this posture of generosity and contentment and living with open hand as if everything is God's,

53
00:04:48,900 --> 00:04:51,000
it's actually for your joy and for your life.

54
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:55,240
So those are some of my disclaimers.

55
00:04:55,240 --> 00:05:00,940
Last week we talked about the natural propensity in the human heart to store up wealth.

56
00:05:00,940 --> 00:05:02,440
We like to put it away.

57
00:05:02,440 --> 00:05:03,540
We like to save it.

58
00:05:03,540 --> 00:05:06,500
And we do this because we want to feel secure.

59
00:05:06,500 --> 00:05:08,020
We want to feel safe.

60
00:05:08,020 --> 00:05:09,700
We want to feel at peace.

61
00:05:10,340 --> 00:05:16,020
And Jesus warned us last week that earthly wealth is futile and subject to the brokenness of this world.

62
00:05:16,020 --> 00:05:18,720
It's where moth and rust destroy.

63
00:05:18,720 --> 00:05:20,100
No matter how much you put away.

64
00:05:20,100 --> 00:05:21,760
No matter how much you save.

65
00:05:21,760 --> 00:05:24,100
No matter how safe you think you are.

66
00:05:24,100 --> 00:05:25,180
This world is broken.

67
00:05:25,180 --> 00:05:28,380
And you'll never accumulate enough.

68
00:05:28,380 --> 00:05:31,960
You'll never store up enough to feel truly safe.

69
00:05:31,960 --> 00:05:38,120
His solution was to store up treasures in heaven by living sacrificially and generously.

70
00:05:40,120 --> 00:05:43,160
And he promises that that mindset will actually lead to life.

71
00:05:43,160 --> 00:05:44,980
So if you missed last week, that's where we were.

72
00:05:45,800 --> 00:05:50,940
And this week we're going to turn our eyes to the natural propensity in the human heart.

73
00:05:50,940 --> 00:05:59,940
Not to store up wealth for safety and security, but to accumulate wealth so that we can spend it for our pleasure and our joy.

74
00:05:59,940 --> 00:06:02,320
So just real quick, a fun survey.

75
00:06:02,320 --> 00:06:06,080
If you would consider yourself a saver, raise your hand.

76
00:06:06,080 --> 00:06:06,700
You're a saver.

77
00:06:08,560 --> 00:06:10,820
Okay, decent amount of us in the room.

78
00:06:10,820 --> 00:06:14,600
So last week's message was probably going to be harder for you than this week's message.

79
00:06:14,600 --> 00:06:16,940
Now, if you're a spender, do me a favor.

80
00:06:16,940 --> 00:06:17,680
Raise your hand.

81
00:06:17,680 --> 00:06:20,200
All right, we got some spenders in the room.

82
00:06:20,200 --> 00:06:20,480
Good.

83
00:06:20,480 --> 00:06:22,880
All right, well, it's your turn to sit on the hot seat.

84
00:06:22,880 --> 00:06:25,000
Last week was the hot seat for savers.

85
00:06:25,620 --> 00:06:31,800
This week is going to be, oh, I think what I hear breaking out right now is husbands and wives who sit on opposite.

86
00:06:31,800 --> 00:06:33,280
Is that what's going on?

87
00:06:33,280 --> 00:06:36,280
We got savers and spenders and they're elbowing each other.

88
00:06:36,280 --> 00:06:37,320
Did you listen last week?

89
00:06:37,320 --> 00:06:38,540
Are you going to listen this week?

90
00:06:38,540 --> 00:06:39,420
All right.

91
00:06:39,420 --> 00:06:40,760
So I like it.

92
00:06:40,760 --> 00:06:44,420
There's a felt need in the room for both talks.

93
00:06:44,420 --> 00:06:49,640
This week, we're going to talk about the desire to accumulate things so that we can spend it.

94
00:06:49,640 --> 00:06:56,680
What does Jesus have to say about this pursuit and what solutions might he give us to fight back against this dangerous temptation?

95
00:06:56,680 --> 00:06:57,940
Does that sound like a good plan?

96
00:06:57,940 --> 00:06:59,380
Awesome.

97
00:06:59,380 --> 00:07:00,040
Let's pray.

98
00:07:00,040 --> 00:07:02,500
Oh, Father in heaven.

99
00:07:02,500 --> 00:07:07,900
Everything we have is yours.

100
00:07:09,820 --> 00:07:14,800
True security, safety, peace, and joy is ultimately found in you.

101
00:07:14,800 --> 00:07:26,120
And yet, day in and day out, moment by moment, we will be tempted and drawn away to believe that we can find our own joy, our own satisfaction, our own peace.

102
00:07:26,120 --> 00:07:33,820
Apart from you, God, every day, every day is placed in our lives.

103
00:07:34,860 --> 00:07:41,860
The tree of the knowledge of good and evil, and we are tempted to believe, not to trust you, but to take a bite from the forbidden tree.

104
00:07:41,860 --> 00:07:51,660
God, may this series be a reminder to us that you truly are a loving father, a good, good father who wants good gifts for us.

105
00:07:51,660 --> 00:07:59,320
May we learn to trust you in the midst of our insecurity and our fear and our greed and our worry.

106
00:08:00,560 --> 00:08:06,280
Holy Spirit, make us believe what is true.

107
00:08:06,280 --> 00:08:10,220
Make us aware of where we are believing things that aren't true.

108
00:08:10,220 --> 00:08:12,460
It's in Jesus' name I pray.

109
00:08:12,460 --> 00:08:13,160
Amen.

110
00:08:13,160 --> 00:08:14,020
Amen.

111
00:08:14,020 --> 00:08:18,600
All right, so a couple months ago, Marissa and I, actually, I guess it was a couple years ago at this point,

112
00:08:18,600 --> 00:08:21,080
Marissa and I were in the market for a new mattress.

113
00:08:21,080 --> 00:08:25,560
And mattress shopping is a pretty serious deal in the Miller household.

114
00:08:25,860 --> 00:08:34,280
We don't spend a pretty penny on a lot of things, but if we're going to spend a majority of our life in a spot, we should probably invest in it, right?

115
00:08:34,280 --> 00:08:38,980
So Marissa and I are debating and looking and sending articles and having this conversation.

116
00:08:38,980 --> 00:08:46,380
And I don't know about you, but when that starts to happen, the rest of my life is inundated with ads for whatever that thing is.

117
00:08:46,380 --> 00:08:48,700
Did any of you ever have this experience?

118
00:08:48,960 --> 00:08:50,720
What's crazy is it's gotten better.

119
00:08:50,720 --> 00:08:58,640
You used to have to at least, like, type it in order for, like, the people who want you to buy their stuff to know that you're looking for their stuff.

120
00:08:58,640 --> 00:09:03,400
Now all you have to do is, like, mention it in a casual conversation to one of your friends, right?

121
00:09:03,480 --> 00:09:09,500
And your feed is filled with advertisements for the thing that you had one conversation about.

122
00:09:09,500 --> 00:09:17,220
For most of us, a huge portion of the content that we engage with on a regular basis, on a daily basis,

123
00:09:17,220 --> 00:09:24,400
is intentionally curated advertisements trying to persuade you to believe that if you just bought the next product,

124
00:09:24,400 --> 00:09:29,840
that if you just went on the next trip, that if you just got the next subscription,

125
00:09:30,640 --> 00:09:32,860
your happiness level would increase.

126
00:09:32,860 --> 00:09:38,460
Executives spend billions of dollars every year on these advertisements.

127
00:09:38,460 --> 00:09:41,420
And these executives, I hate to break it to you,

128
00:09:41,420 --> 00:09:45,000
they're pretty smart and they're good at numbers.

129
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:47,700
They would not invest the money if it didn't work.

130
00:09:47,700 --> 00:09:50,640
They're spending this money because it's working.

131
00:09:50,640 --> 00:09:55,540
It is persuading us to believe the messaging that they are teaching us.

132
00:09:55,600 --> 00:10:01,060
We are being more discipled by advertisements than we are by the Son of God who came,

133
00:10:01,060 --> 00:10:04,300
lived a perfect life, and taught us how to view our stuff.

134
00:10:04,300 --> 00:10:08,300
The human heart is prone to believe this myth of more.

135
00:10:08,300 --> 00:10:13,360
We look at people above us on the economic ladder and we think,

136
00:10:13,360 --> 00:10:21,140
if I had that car, those clothes, that house, that pool, that membership, or took that trip,

137
00:10:21,140 --> 00:10:22,800
then I would be happy.

138
00:10:22,800 --> 00:10:24,580
Then I would be content.

139
00:10:24,580 --> 00:10:25,880
And here's the crazy part.

140
00:10:25,880 --> 00:10:31,380
The maddening part as a pastor, and just as a human being really,

141
00:10:31,380 --> 00:10:33,500
is the people that you were looking at,

142
00:10:33,500 --> 00:10:39,020
they're looking at the person one step above them in the economic ladder,

143
00:10:39,020 --> 00:10:42,200
and they're thinking, well, if I had that car, that house,

144
00:10:42,200 --> 00:10:45,400
if I was able to go on that trip or join that club,

145
00:10:45,400 --> 00:10:47,940
then I would be happy.

146
00:10:47,940 --> 00:10:51,820
Psychologists call this the hedonic treadmill.

147
00:10:51,820 --> 00:10:54,920
Constantly chasing pleasure.

148
00:10:54,920 --> 00:10:57,680
We hop on the treadmill and we are chasing pleasure.

149
00:10:57,680 --> 00:11:04,380
And yet we arrive nowhere and become exhausted in the process.

150
00:11:04,380 --> 00:11:07,560
And all of my people who don't like to work out are like,

151
00:11:07,560 --> 00:11:09,420
yeah, that's why I stay away from the treadmill.

152
00:11:09,420 --> 00:11:12,140
It's pointless, right?

153
00:11:12,140 --> 00:11:14,820
You get on, you get off, you went nowhere, and you're tired.

154
00:11:14,820 --> 00:11:20,480
This is what we're doing, many of us, as we view our finances.

155
00:11:20,480 --> 00:11:23,920
And the crazy thing is it's not a modern phenomenon.

156
00:11:23,920 --> 00:11:28,680
It's not the executives that are convincing us to do something that humans have never done before.

157
00:11:28,680 --> 00:11:34,340
Listen to the words of Solomon, one of the wisest men who ever lived a few thousand years ago.

158
00:11:34,380 --> 00:11:39,100
He says this, those who love money will never have enough.

159
00:11:39,100 --> 00:11:45,620
How meaningless to think that wealth brings true happiness.

160
00:11:45,620 --> 00:11:52,260
And all of my spenders said, can we get an intermission so I can go to the bathroom and not come back?

161
00:11:52,260 --> 00:11:53,760
Right?

162
00:11:54,480 --> 00:12:00,960
So, with all that in mind, it should not come to a surprise to us that many of Christ's teachings about money,

163
00:12:00,960 --> 00:12:07,240
remember we said last week that Christ, a lot of scholars think that up to 25% of Jesus' teachings are about our money and our possessions.

164
00:12:09,080 --> 00:12:20,220
And in that breakdown, it shouldn't be a surprise to us that a lot of what Jesus has to say about our money is less about what we do with what we have and more about avoiding this myth of more.

165
00:12:20,220 --> 00:12:23,520
More about avoiding buying into the next thing.

166
00:12:23,520 --> 00:12:27,140
The more you get, the better your life will be.

167
00:12:27,140 --> 00:12:33,240
Let's quickly take a look at three of Christ's warnings about this idea of getting more.

168
00:12:33,240 --> 00:12:39,760
Look, in Luke chapter 12, verse 15, his first warning is that greed is dangerous.

169
00:12:39,760 --> 00:12:41,380
Greed is dangerous.

170
00:12:41,380 --> 00:12:43,280
In Luke chapter 12, verse 15, he says,

171
00:12:43,280 --> 00:12:48,420
Beware, guard against every kind of greed.

172
00:12:49,780 --> 00:12:56,420
I don't know about you, but when Jesus says something with an exclamation point, I'm going to listen a little bit more intently, right?

173
00:12:56,420 --> 00:13:03,500
Like, he is emphatic about this, beware, be on guard, look out for every kind of greed in your life.

174
00:13:03,500 --> 00:13:09,480
I love how John Mark Homer, the author of the Practicing the Way curriculum, defines greed.

175
00:13:09,480 --> 00:13:12,980
He says, greed is a lusting for things.

176
00:13:12,980 --> 00:13:15,860
A lusting for things.

177
00:13:15,860 --> 00:13:19,260
It is a transactional interaction between us and stuff.

178
00:13:19,260 --> 00:13:23,460
And we think the more stuff we get, the more experiences we have, the more things we accumulate,

179
00:13:23,460 --> 00:13:27,920
then that longing in our heart will be satisfied.

180
00:13:27,920 --> 00:13:29,480
It's a form of idolatry.

181
00:13:29,480 --> 00:13:35,020
It takes things and puts them on the same level as God or higher in our hearts.

182
00:13:35,020 --> 00:13:39,520
And we can see how this relationship might be dangerous, right?

183
00:13:39,520 --> 00:13:45,380
When we elevate things in our life, it has the power to do a lot of damage.

184
00:13:45,380 --> 00:13:47,060
And this is Christ's warning.

185
00:13:47,060 --> 00:13:49,500
He says, beware, look out for it.

186
00:13:49,500 --> 00:13:50,460
It's dangerous.

187
00:13:50,460 --> 00:13:57,660
As a matter of fact, the statement that Jesus makes here, I'm just going to leave it there because every time I try and fix it, I get louder.

188
00:13:57,660 --> 00:13:58,980
Good?

189
00:13:58,980 --> 00:13:59,380
Okay.

190
00:13:59,380 --> 00:14:06,500
The statement that Jesus makes here is in response to a young man who comes to Jesus, right?

191
00:14:06,500 --> 00:14:07,980
A teacher of the Scriptures.

192
00:14:07,980 --> 00:14:11,740
And this man comes to Jesus and he says, tell my brother to share the inheritance with me.

193
00:14:13,660 --> 00:14:20,860
Now, is Jesus responding to his question at all or is he doing what Jesus does and ignoring the question and getting to the root of the guy's issue?

194
00:14:20,860 --> 00:14:23,020
That was a hypothetical question.

195
00:14:23,020 --> 00:14:26,440
He's ignoring the guy's question and getting to the root of the issue.

196
00:14:26,440 --> 00:14:30,080
He says, beware, guard against every kind of greed.

197
00:14:30,140 --> 00:14:38,100
I think what Jesus is doing here is he's helping the guy see your desire for wealth, your desire for more is putting you at odds with your brother.

198
00:14:39,100 --> 00:14:42,660
This relationship that should be far more important than stuff.

199
00:14:42,660 --> 00:14:50,200
You're coming to me and you're trying to convince me to tell your brother what he should do with the money that's been entrusted to him.

200
00:14:50,200 --> 00:14:58,780
The greed in your heart is actually causing you to value stuff over the people that you're in familial relationship with.

201
00:14:58,780 --> 00:15:04,980
It's important that we notice that there are multiple forms of greed.

202
00:15:06,780 --> 00:15:17,060
I don't know about you, but I am very good at noticing greed in other people's lives, especially people who are greedy for things that I think are silly.

203
00:15:17,060 --> 00:15:19,920
Am I the only one?

204
00:15:19,920 --> 00:15:21,120
Yes.

205
00:15:21,120 --> 00:15:29,800
Man, the more Jay gets to know me, the more comfortable he feels heckling me in the middle of a sermon.

206
00:15:29,800 --> 00:15:32,360
Right?

207
00:15:32,360 --> 00:15:36,160
Like, I look at people who lust for cars.

208
00:15:36,540 --> 00:15:39,260
Like, if it runs, it works for me.

209
00:15:39,260 --> 00:15:39,600
Right?

210
00:15:39,600 --> 00:15:40,360
I'm not a car guy.

211
00:15:40,360 --> 00:15:44,680
And so I look at people who lust for cars and I'm like, they are greedy.

212
00:15:44,680 --> 00:15:46,620
How dare they?

213
00:15:46,620 --> 00:15:51,780
How dare they view such a thing as bringing them value in life?

214
00:15:51,780 --> 00:15:58,340
And then I get an invitation to a private golf club once a week at $120 a clip.

215
00:15:58,340 --> 00:15:59,240
And I'm like, you know what?

216
00:15:59,240 --> 00:15:59,980
I work hard.

217
00:16:02,720 --> 00:16:05,040
I could move some money around here.

218
00:16:05,040 --> 00:16:05,680
Right?

219
00:16:05,680 --> 00:16:07,300
I could find it.

220
00:16:07,300 --> 00:16:07,660
Really?

221
00:16:07,660 --> 00:16:08,000
Right?

222
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:11,520
Like, I could find some cash and it wouldn't be that big of a deal.

223
00:16:11,520 --> 00:16:15,200
We tend to demonize people who are greedy for things that we find silly.

224
00:16:16,160 --> 00:16:19,280
Meanwhile, we justify our own greediness.

225
00:16:19,280 --> 00:16:25,100
We should all heed Jesus' warnings to be on guard against every kind of greed in our lives.

226
00:16:25,100 --> 00:16:30,540
And focus more on the kind that's in your life and not the kind that's in your neighbor's life.

227
00:16:32,220 --> 00:16:34,440
So, what are some things that you're lusting after?

228
00:16:34,440 --> 00:16:38,320
What are some products or experiences you daydream about getting?

229
00:16:38,320 --> 00:16:43,500
What things do you already have that consume much of your time, energy, and resources?

230
00:16:43,500 --> 00:16:47,320
Greed is dangerous, says Christ.

231
00:16:47,320 --> 00:16:50,260
The second thing he says is that greed is deceitful.

232
00:16:50,260 --> 00:16:55,060
He says that he's talking about the parable of the sower of the seeds.

233
00:16:55,060 --> 00:16:58,520
He's explaining it to the disciples because they didn't know what the heck he was talking about.

234
00:16:58,520 --> 00:17:02,340
I don't know if you've read the Gospels lately, but they often didn't know what the heck he was talking about.

235
00:17:02,340 --> 00:17:05,680
And sometimes he was gracious enough to explain it to them.

236
00:17:05,680 --> 00:17:08,600
And other times he was like, it's not worth it.

237
00:17:08,600 --> 00:17:09,400
You'll figure it out later.

238
00:17:09,400 --> 00:17:09,820
It's fine.

239
00:17:09,820 --> 00:17:13,200
So, this is one of those times where he was explaining it to them.

240
00:17:13,200 --> 00:17:15,120
And he says,

241
00:17:15,120 --> 00:17:19,300
The seed that fell among the thorns represents those who hear God's word.

242
00:17:19,300 --> 00:17:24,200
But all too quickly, the message is crowded out by the worries of this life.

243
00:17:24,200 --> 00:17:25,020
Listen to this.

244
00:17:25,480 --> 00:17:38,060
This is an individual who has received the message of the kingdom of God.

245
00:17:38,060 --> 00:17:45,040
That a loving father creator has initiated a relationship with them.

246
00:17:45,040 --> 00:17:48,820
That they can live for eternal things rather than temporary things.

247
00:17:48,820 --> 00:17:52,460
The greatest message on earth has been given to them.

248
00:17:52,460 --> 00:17:53,820
And they have received it.

249
00:17:53,820 --> 00:18:06,600
And yet, after a little bit of time, this idea of eternity mattering more than temporary things is choked out by their desire for more stuff.

250
00:18:06,600 --> 00:18:08,640
The lure of wealth.

251
00:18:09,720 --> 00:18:11,200
Jesus says, greed is deceitful.

252
00:18:11,200 --> 00:18:14,920
It convinces you that what is less important is more important.

253
00:18:14,920 --> 00:18:21,800
It convinces us that temporary things are more important than eternal things.

254
00:18:21,800 --> 00:18:22,520
Is it possible?

255
00:18:22,520 --> 00:18:27,680
Some of us in this room have intellectually received the message of the kingdom of God.

256
00:18:27,680 --> 00:18:29,740
We agree with it.

257
00:18:29,740 --> 00:18:30,700
We believe it.

258
00:18:31,980 --> 00:18:37,960
And yet, if you look at our lives, our lives are more concerned with the lure of wealth and the desire for things.

259
00:18:37,960 --> 00:18:46,780
Jesus says, the proper response to the kingdom of God is not, yep, that's great.

260
00:18:46,780 --> 00:18:47,360
I love it.

261
00:18:47,360 --> 00:18:48,360
Stuff.

262
00:18:48,360 --> 00:18:51,700
He says, the proper response to the kingdom of God is this.

263
00:18:51,780 --> 00:18:55,680
The kingdom of heaven is like a treasure that a man discovered hidden in a field.

264
00:18:55,680 --> 00:19:02,740
In his excitement, he hid it again and he sold everything that he owned to get enough money to buy the field.

265
00:19:02,740 --> 00:19:09,740
The kingdom of God is so much more valuable than any lure of wealth or desire for more things.

266
00:19:09,740 --> 00:19:12,700
And yet, it lies to us.

267
00:19:12,700 --> 00:19:15,040
Stuff lies to us.

268
00:19:15,040 --> 00:19:18,920
It causes us to believe that it's more important than it actually is.

269
00:19:19,300 --> 00:19:26,420
And we end up wasting our life chasing after things rather than investing in the kingdom of God, which will last forever.

270
00:19:26,420 --> 00:19:32,460
We make bad investments for short-term gain.

271
00:19:32,460 --> 00:19:36,880
Greed is dangerous.

272
00:19:36,880 --> 00:19:38,680
It's deceitful.

273
00:19:38,680 --> 00:19:40,600
And the third thing he says is it's distracting.

274
00:19:40,600 --> 00:19:47,600
Jesus said to his disciples, I tell you the truth, it is very hard for a rich person to enter the kingdom of heaven.

275
00:19:47,600 --> 00:19:48,540
I'll say it again.

276
00:19:49,300 --> 00:19:55,320
It is easier for a camel to go through the eye of a needle than for a rich person to enter the kingdom of God.

277
00:19:55,320 --> 00:20:01,280
This is probably one of Christ's hardest-hitting statements about wealth and greed.

278
00:20:01,280 --> 00:20:07,540
And most of us in the room, when we hear it, are thinking about a person and economic status above us.

279
00:20:07,540 --> 00:20:10,700
None of us think that we're rich.

280
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:12,180
Right?

281
00:20:12,180 --> 00:20:18,080
But in this Jewish context, rich meant you had access to food and clothing and shelter.

282
00:20:18,080 --> 00:20:19,840
Right?

283
00:20:19,840 --> 00:20:29,480
If you have access, this should be a warning to all of us, most of us, most of us in this room have access to the earthly resources we need.

284
00:20:29,480 --> 00:20:31,060
Food, shelter, clothing.

285
00:20:32,000 --> 00:20:41,440
Access to earthly resources distracts us from seeking the kingdom of God, from seeing the kingdom of God as more valuable than accumulating earthly possessions.

286
00:20:41,440 --> 00:20:43,240
It's distracting.

287
00:20:44,700 --> 00:20:48,680
I had a friend who was a youth pastor a few years back in Cary, North Carolina.

288
00:20:48,680 --> 00:20:50,160
Anybody ever heard of Cary, North Carolina?

289
00:20:50,160 --> 00:20:52,740
Apparently, I've been there once.

290
00:20:52,740 --> 00:20:55,740
Apparently, it's like one of the wealthiest counties in the country.

291
00:20:55,740 --> 00:20:58,920
It's like the tech triangle, research triangle of Carolina.

292
00:20:59,100 --> 00:21:03,620
And he was talking about how every single one of his students are rich.

293
00:21:03,620 --> 00:21:04,740
They're loaded.

294
00:21:04,740 --> 00:21:08,080
They all drive like Mercedes and BMWs to high school.

295
00:21:08,080 --> 00:21:08,520
It's crazy.

296
00:21:08,520 --> 00:21:11,260
And I'll never forget the line that he told me.

297
00:21:11,260 --> 00:21:12,320
He looked me in the eye.

298
00:21:12,320 --> 00:21:14,820
I was talking to him about how ministry is going, how church is going.

299
00:21:14,820 --> 00:21:16,300
He looked me in the eye and he said,

300
00:21:16,300 --> 00:21:21,080
Try telling kids who have never needed anything in their entire life that they need Jesus.

301
00:21:21,080 --> 00:21:25,740
This is the distracting nature of stuff.

302
00:21:26,500 --> 00:21:29,340
Those of us that have access to more than enough things,

303
00:21:29,340 --> 00:21:33,000
we lose sight of what matters most.

304
00:21:33,000 --> 00:21:37,500
The more stuff we have, the more stuff we accumulate, the more distracted we get.

305
00:21:37,500 --> 00:21:45,200
The more we're pulled in to invest in temporary earthly pleasures rather than the kingdom of God.

306
00:21:45,200 --> 00:21:52,480
Most of us in this room, we have access to more than the basic necessities of life,

307
00:21:52,480 --> 00:21:54,060
which would put us in the category of rich.

308
00:21:54,120 --> 00:22:00,420
We should take this warning seriously, not to let wealth distract us from his kingdom.

309
00:22:00,420 --> 00:22:05,260
Now, if you're depressed, take a deep breath.

310
00:22:05,260 --> 00:22:07,680
Thank you.

311
00:22:07,680 --> 00:22:09,280
Me and Jay are depressed up here.

312
00:22:09,280 --> 00:22:10,020
All right.

313
00:22:10,020 --> 00:22:11,420
There's good news.

314
00:22:11,420 --> 00:22:13,020
There's good news.

315
00:22:13,180 --> 00:22:17,420
He goes on to say that it's not impossible that anything is possible with God.

316
00:22:17,420 --> 00:22:22,000
And Americans, we need to hold tight to this truth that by the power of the Holy Spirit,

317
00:22:22,000 --> 00:22:28,520
those of us in the room who are most of us, who have access to a lot,

318
00:22:28,520 --> 00:22:31,840
we don't necessarily have to sell everything we have to live in God's kingdom,

319
00:22:31,840 --> 00:22:36,720
but we need to seek to submit everything we have to his purposes.

320
00:22:37,240 --> 00:22:40,460
By the power of the Holy Spirit, with a personal relationship with the Spirit,

321
00:22:40,460 --> 00:22:44,880
we can steward the things that God has given us in a way that builds into his kingdom

322
00:22:44,880 --> 00:22:48,560
and keeps us focused on what is most important in life.

323
00:22:52,380 --> 00:22:54,800
At this point, you might be thinking, I love when I write this.

324
00:22:54,800 --> 00:22:57,480
I have to read this in my notes because I think I'm funnier than I am.

325
00:22:57,480 --> 00:23:02,880
At this point, you might be thinking, does Jesus just warn against the dangers of greed

326
00:23:02,880 --> 00:23:07,380
or does he offer any practical wisdom on how to avoid greed in our lives?

327
00:23:07,380 --> 00:23:10,020
I'm so glad you guys asked that question.

328
00:23:10,020 --> 00:23:16,300
The first passage we looked at in Luke chapter 12,

329
00:23:16,300 --> 00:23:20,420
I stopped it in the middle because I'm cheeky and now I'm going to give you the rest.

330
00:23:20,420 --> 00:23:23,740
Also, I've been watching a lot of Bluey,

331
00:23:23,740 --> 00:23:25,840
so you're going to hear me say cheeky a lot more.

332
00:23:25,840 --> 00:23:28,700
Welcome to fatherhood.

333
00:23:28,700 --> 00:23:29,100
Okay.

334
00:23:29,100 --> 00:23:32,300
Here is the rest of the verse we started with.

335
00:23:32,300 --> 00:23:34,660
Beware, guard against every kind of greed.

336
00:23:34,660 --> 00:23:38,520
Life is not measured by how much you own.

337
00:23:38,520 --> 00:23:40,680
He goes on in Matthew 6,

338
00:23:40,680 --> 00:23:43,140
Seek the kingdom of God above all else and live righteously

339
00:23:43,140 --> 00:23:45,840
and he will give you everything you need.

340
00:23:46,620 --> 00:23:51,340
The word used to describe this attitude towards stuff is called contentment.

341
00:23:51,340 --> 00:23:54,000
And it is the opposite of greed.

342
00:23:54,000 --> 00:24:00,840
This is Jesus' solution for those of us who are tempted to live after the desires of our heart,

343
00:24:00,840 --> 00:24:02,560
to seek pleasure in earthly things.

344
00:24:02,560 --> 00:24:05,680
He says that if we want to fight against that,

345
00:24:05,680 --> 00:24:09,580
if we want to truly live for the kingdom of God on earth as it is in heaven,

346
00:24:09,580 --> 00:24:15,020
we've got to learn to be content with what we have and invest what we have in the kingdom.

347
00:24:15,020 --> 00:24:20,120
I love how Randy Alcorn defines contentment.

348
00:24:20,120 --> 00:24:24,300
He says contentment is being satisfied in whose you are,

349
00:24:24,300 --> 00:24:25,760
who you are,

350
00:24:25,760 --> 00:24:27,740
and what you have.

351
00:24:28,560 --> 00:24:38,240
This is the goal for followers of Jesus,

352
00:24:38,240 --> 00:24:44,340
that we would learn to be satisfied as children of God,

353
00:24:44,340 --> 00:24:48,240
loved, adopted, brought into the family of God,

354
00:24:48,240 --> 00:24:51,900
that we have everything that we need in him.

355
00:24:54,580 --> 00:24:57,880
See, at the heart of much of our greed is the desire to be happy or satisfied,

356
00:24:57,880 --> 00:24:59,520
so we jump on the hedonic treadmill,

357
00:24:59,520 --> 00:25:01,020
chasing after our desires,

358
00:25:01,020 --> 00:25:01,900
and we get nowhere,

359
00:25:01,900 --> 00:25:03,960
and we're exhausted.

360
00:25:03,960 --> 00:25:06,680
So if greed is like a treadmill,

361
00:25:06,680 --> 00:25:08,240
contentment is like a recliner.

362
00:25:08,240 --> 00:25:09,540
That's pretty good.

363
00:25:09,540 --> 00:25:09,980
Come on.

364
00:25:09,980 --> 00:25:11,480
All right.

365
00:25:11,480 --> 00:25:12,860
Thank you, thank you, thank you.

366
00:25:12,860 --> 00:25:18,940
If greed is like a treadmill,

367
00:25:18,940 --> 00:25:20,060
contentment is like a recliner,

368
00:25:20,060 --> 00:25:23,400
let's learn to find rest and be satisfied in God.

369
00:25:23,400 --> 00:25:26,600
I want to look at what the Apostle Paul has to say about contentment

370
00:25:26,600 --> 00:25:27,900
in 1 Timothy chapter 6.

371
00:25:27,900 --> 00:25:29,460
If you want to follow along with me,

372
00:25:29,460 --> 00:25:32,280
we're going to read a couple of paragraphs from 1 Timothy chapter 6

373
00:25:32,280 --> 00:25:37,280
as we start to get practical about how not to chase greed

374
00:25:37,280 --> 00:25:38,760
and to find contentment.

375
00:25:38,760 --> 00:25:42,340
1 Timothy 6, verses 6 through 8.

376
00:25:42,340 --> 00:25:45,380
Paul says,

377
00:25:45,380 --> 00:25:51,140
True godliness with contentment is itself great wealth.

378
00:25:51,920 --> 00:25:54,500
After all, we brought nothing with us

379
00:25:54,500 --> 00:25:56,560
when we came into the world,

380
00:25:56,560 --> 00:25:59,680
and we can take nothing with us when we leave it.

381
00:25:59,680 --> 00:26:02,940
So if we have enough food and enough clothing,

382
00:26:02,940 --> 00:26:05,140
we should be content.

383
00:26:05,140 --> 00:26:09,860
I love how Paul defines contentment here.

384
00:26:09,860 --> 00:26:12,680
He says that contentment is great wealth.

385
00:26:14,120 --> 00:26:17,520
This is the opposite of what we think about great wealth, right?

386
00:26:17,520 --> 00:26:20,560
We think more stuff equals great wealth.

387
00:26:20,560 --> 00:26:24,380
Paul says being satisfied with what you have

388
00:26:24,380 --> 00:26:27,780
is actually the only way to experience true wealth.

389
00:26:27,780 --> 00:26:30,480
True wealth is learning to be content with what you have.

390
00:26:30,580 --> 00:26:32,560
He quotes the famous passage from Job.

391
00:26:32,560 --> 00:26:34,220
Naked I came from my mother's womb,

392
00:26:34,220 --> 00:26:35,540
and naked I shall return.

393
00:26:35,540 --> 00:26:39,540
We all know this concept in our heads, right?

394
00:26:39,540 --> 00:26:42,100
We know that we've all heard the illustration

395
00:26:42,100 --> 00:26:45,600
that you've never seen a hearse hauling a U-Haul, right?

396
00:26:45,600 --> 00:26:46,360
Like, we know it.

397
00:26:46,360 --> 00:26:47,740
You can't take your stuff with you.

398
00:26:47,740 --> 00:26:49,220
It doesn't come with you.

399
00:26:49,220 --> 00:26:53,600
We look at the Egyptians who bury their princes

400
00:26:53,600 --> 00:26:56,140
in pyramids full of stuff,

401
00:26:56,140 --> 00:26:59,080
and we're like, that's silly and outdated and crazy,

402
00:26:59,080 --> 00:27:01,040
and yet we look at our lives.

403
00:27:01,040 --> 00:27:02,000
I look at my life.

404
00:27:02,000 --> 00:27:06,160
Do I actually live as if nothing I have is coming with me,

405
00:27:06,160 --> 00:27:09,580
or do I keep pursuing the next thing and the next thing

406
00:27:09,580 --> 00:27:11,080
in hopes that it will satisfy me?

407
00:27:11,080 --> 00:27:13,360
We all know this concept to be true,

408
00:27:13,360 --> 00:27:16,880
but many of us rarely let it impact the way we live.

409
00:27:19,220 --> 00:27:21,640
Nothing we accumulate for ourselves on earth

410
00:27:21,640 --> 00:27:23,100
is coming with us,

411
00:27:23,100 --> 00:27:24,800
so why should we make it the focal point

412
00:27:24,800 --> 00:27:25,920
of so much of our activity?

413
00:27:25,920 --> 00:27:29,000
One of my favorite verses in the Bible,

414
00:27:29,000 --> 00:27:31,560
Ecclesiastes chapter three, verse 11.

415
00:27:31,560 --> 00:27:35,320
God has placed eternity in your heart.

416
00:27:35,320 --> 00:27:39,320
There's this void inside of each one of us.

417
00:27:39,320 --> 00:27:41,840
We were created for eternal things.

418
00:27:41,840 --> 00:27:43,840
It's why the message of the kingdom of God

419
00:27:43,840 --> 00:27:46,320
is the most important message in all of human history.

420
00:27:46,800 --> 00:27:49,980
It's that heaven is coming back to earth,

421
00:27:49,980 --> 00:27:53,920
that we can exist for all of eternity

422
00:27:53,920 --> 00:27:55,340
in relationship with God,

423
00:27:55,340 --> 00:27:58,640
that we can begin to live for eternal things now.

424
00:27:58,640 --> 00:28:02,480
God has placed eternity in your heart,

425
00:28:02,480 --> 00:28:05,220
and that is why nothing earthly you ever think

426
00:28:05,220 --> 00:28:07,560
will satisfy you, satisfies you.

427
00:28:13,560 --> 00:28:17,340
Contentment is learning to be satisfied with what you have.

428
00:28:17,340 --> 00:28:20,140
I love what Paul says in 2 Corinthians 12.

429
00:28:20,140 --> 00:28:20,560
He says,

430
00:28:20,560 --> 00:28:21,220
My grace,

431
00:28:21,220 --> 00:28:22,980
this is Jesus speaking to Paul,

432
00:28:22,980 --> 00:28:25,800
My grace is all that you need.

433
00:28:25,800 --> 00:28:28,540
My power works best in weakness.

434
00:28:28,540 --> 00:28:31,000
Jesus tells Paul,

435
00:28:31,000 --> 00:28:32,980
Don't worry about living in poverty.

436
00:28:32,980 --> 00:28:34,820
Don't worry about having a physical ailment.

437
00:28:34,820 --> 00:28:37,180
Don't worry about me not answering the prayer

438
00:28:37,180 --> 00:28:38,260
that you want me to answer.

439
00:28:38,260 --> 00:28:40,260
My grace is all that you need.

440
00:28:40,680 --> 00:28:41,860
I will sustain you.

441
00:28:41,860 --> 00:28:43,100
I will satisfy you.

442
00:28:43,100 --> 00:28:45,680
True contentment can only be found

443
00:28:45,680 --> 00:28:48,260
when we accept that we are eternal beings

444
00:28:48,260 --> 00:28:49,540
created for eternal purposes,

445
00:28:49,540 --> 00:28:52,400
and no earthly possession will ever satisfy

446
00:28:52,400 --> 00:28:54,140
the deepest longings of our heart.

447
00:28:54,140 --> 00:28:55,800
He goes on.

448
00:28:55,800 --> 00:28:57,040
Verse 9,

449
00:28:57,140 --> 00:28:59,180
But people who long to be rich

450
00:28:59,180 --> 00:29:01,420
fall into temptation

451
00:29:01,420 --> 00:29:04,240
and are trapped by many foolish and harmful desires

452
00:29:04,240 --> 00:29:07,240
that plunge them into ruin and destruction.

453
00:29:07,240 --> 00:29:11,660
For the love of money is the root of all kinds of evil,

454
00:29:11,660 --> 00:29:13,200
and some people,

455
00:29:13,200 --> 00:29:13,780
listen to this,

456
00:29:13,780 --> 00:29:15,680
craving money,

457
00:29:15,680 --> 00:29:18,580
craving money,

458
00:29:18,580 --> 00:29:20,840
have wandered from the true faith

459
00:29:20,840 --> 00:29:23,740
and pierced themselves with many sorrows.

460
00:29:26,460 --> 00:29:28,480
I'm not going to spend a whole lot of time here

461
00:29:28,480 --> 00:29:30,260
because I think what we can see here

462
00:29:30,260 --> 00:29:31,360
is that Paul is recapping

463
00:29:31,360 --> 00:29:33,220
a lot of what Jesus already said about greed.

464
00:29:33,220 --> 00:29:34,320
It's dangerous.

465
00:29:34,320 --> 00:29:35,200
It's deceitful.

466
00:29:35,200 --> 00:29:36,560
It's distracting.

467
00:29:36,560 --> 00:29:39,340
It leads us to all kinds of sorrows.

468
00:29:39,340 --> 00:29:44,740
Verse 10.

469
00:29:44,740 --> 00:29:45,920
I want to read that again.

470
00:29:48,800 --> 00:29:51,640
For the love of money is the root of all kinds of evil,

471
00:29:51,640 --> 00:29:53,160
and some people craving money

472
00:29:53,160 --> 00:29:54,540
have wandered from the true faith

473
00:29:54,540 --> 00:29:58,000
and pierced themselves with many sorrows.

474
00:29:58,000 --> 00:30:01,260
It's important here that we point out

475
00:30:01,260 --> 00:30:04,100
that it's not just the pursuit of money

476
00:30:04,100 --> 00:30:05,640
that leads to many sorrows.

477
00:30:05,640 --> 00:30:10,760
